  "definitions": {
    "language_id": "primary language of each record's text by naltra.pipeline.language.LinguaLanguageDetector (lingua restricted to EN and TR; minimum confidence 0.6, minimum share 0.2): en-tr when both languages hold at least 2 words and that share of the confidently detected words, und under 2 words or below that confidence",
    "not_tr, not_en": "records not detected as their own language; examples are the first 5 in file order",
    "round_trip": "300 TR test records drawn by random.Random(seed).sample from the sorted record ids, plus every TR test record a translation_checks screen flags; each stored TR aligned sentence is translated back to English with the pinned model and the sentences are joined with spaces",
    "chrf": "document chrF (Popovic 2015) of the back-translation against the EN source text: character n-grams of orders 1..6 with whitespace removed, clipped matches, precision and recall averaged over the orders, F-beta with beta = 2, 0-100; chrf, below_40, below_30 and lowest cover the sample only",
    "screens": "mean chrF of every TR test record each translation_checks screen flags (in_sample: how many are in the sample) and of the sampled records no screen flags",
    "scope": "round-trip chrF is an automatic proxy, not a human judgement: errors of the EN->TR release model can cancel out or be introduced by the reverse model, and chrF measures character overlap with the EN source, not Turkish fluency; language ID shows a record reads as Turkish, not that it is a faithful translation"
  },
